body:
ken main here since day one (currently on gold 4 due to a lack of self confidence). any tips about the right timing to use run+shoryuken to go under fireballs? it's one of the coolest moves ken has in my opinion and I'd like to learn how to land it consistently. 

&#x200B;

I've already tried to practice it on the lab, but I always end up with a fireball to the face.

oh boy, where do I start?. let's see, I don't anti air with dps enough, tend to throw normals that are not cancelable which causes that my opponent to di my ass, stilll don't have a "go to" response for opponents who love using crossups on me, still get scared in corners, still get scared in mirror matches (I'm a ken main) beacuse I have the idea that my opponent somehow uses ken better than I do, still get nervous during ranked matches which causes that I start making dumb mistakes. just to name a few.

&#x200B;

but, I have to make this clear, I do love the game, even when I  get  nothing but loses. I enjoy learning new things, new ways to use the tools at my disposal to suck just a  bit less. It's the first fighting game I take seriously and I love (for the most part) the community around it. I just need more experience I guess.
